WAF:(web application firewall) 
→ it works like a firewall. Firewall works on layer 3 and layer 4 in the osi model. main aim of firewall= block malicious and unauthorized traffic.
→ a web application firewall is an application level firewall for HTTP applications.
→ it applies a set of rules for the http based conversions.
→ WAF generally are deployed to protect against attacks targeted towards applications, specifically the ones defined in the OWASP top 10 metrics.
→ there are a lot of ways in which you can implement WAF and various vendors as well.
→ NAXSI and modsecurity are some of the famous open source ones.
→ Signal science, Akamai and AWS WAF are some of the commercial vendors that offer WAF related functionalities.
→ web acl → association → rules → rule statements
→ rule statement: rules statements define basic characteristics that would be analyzed within a web request. These can be custom-defined or you can use ready-made ones from aws and marketplace.
Block all the requests which are coming from out of india.(geolocation)
Block request which has a url path of admin.
You can even build custom conditions based on: 
headers, HTTP method, Query strings, URL path, geo-location, body.
→ rules: we can combine multiple statements into rules to precisely target requests. WAF provides two primary rules types : regular rule & rate-based rule.
Sample regular rule:
If a request comes from 172.30.0.50
Request has sql like code
Rules with multiple statements can be AND, OR , NOT
        Sample rate-based rule= regular rule + rate limiting feature
If a request comes from 172.30.0.50
If a request exceeds 1000 requests in 10 minutes
→associations: association defines which entity WAF is associated with.
Waf can't be associated with ec2 instances directly. 
 It can associate only ALB (application load balancer), Cloud front, and api gateway.
→ web ACL: web acl is a centralized place that contains the rules, rule statements and associated configuration. It is used as a protection strategy.
IMPORTANT  POINTS:
Rules can be configured which have multiple rules that can be used across multiple web acls.
Customers can decide to use ready-made aws managed rules or even rules from aws marketplace.
Every rule has a priority. If a request matches priority 0 rule, none of the other rules will inspect the request.
Pricing aspect: web-acl ($5 per month, rule ($1 per month), requests($0.60 for 1 million)
