Explain the Shared Responsibility Model in AWS.?
Answer: The Shared Responsibility Model in AWS delineates the security functions provided by AWS (security of the cloud) and those that must be managed by the customer (security in the cloud). AWS is responsible for protecting the infrastructure that runs AWS services, including hardware, software, networking, and facilities. Customers are responsible for managing their data, identity and access management, operating systems, network and firewall configurations, application security, and data encryption.
