                                       Terraform provisioner
A Terraform provisioner is a feature used to execute scripts or commands on a resource after it has been created, during the terraform apply process. Provisioners are typically used to perform tasks such as software installation, configuration, or running scripts that are not directly handled by Terraform’s resource management.
Types of Provisioners
local-exec: Executes a command on the machine where Terraform is running.
provisioner "local-exec" {
  command = "echo Hello, world!"
}
remote-exec: Executes a command on the remote resource after it has been created. Typically used with cloud instances.
provisioner "remote-exec" {
  inline = [
    "sudo apt-get update",
    "sudo apt-get install -y nginx"
  ]

  connection {
    type        = "ssh"
    host        = self.public_ip
    user        = "ubuntu"
    private_key = file("~/.ssh/id_rsa")
  }
}
