✅ Quality Gate (in SonarQube):
A set of conditions that a project must meet to be considered "clean" or "healthy".
Examples:
No critical bugs , Code coverage ≥ 80% ,  Duplications < 5%
Result: Pass or Fail (used in CI/CD pipelines to block bad code)
✅ Quality Profile (in SonarQube):
A collection of coding rules applied during code analysis.
Different profiles for different languages (e.g., Java, Python).
You can customize or use default profiles (e.g., Sonar Way).
