3) Which arguments do we use in the Docker file?
 🡪 FORM=to pull the base image
ex:FROM ubuntu:latest
 🡪 LABEL= here we mention version and date and who maintain file like this
ex:  LABEL maintainer=”venkat” version=”1.0.0” date=”29/9/2024”
 🡪 RUN =to execute linux commands
ex: RUN apt-get -y update -y && apt-get -y upgrade -y
CMD= container execution time use default commands
ex: CMD ["/opt/tomcat/bin/catalina.sh", "run"]
ENTRYPOINT=to configure a container that will run as executables(same as cmd) ex:ENTRYPOINT ["node", "index.js"]
WORKDIR=to set working directory first create directory using run #RUN mkdir /opt/tomcat
ex: WORKDIR opt/tomcat
COPY=to copy the directory from local machine to container
ex: ./index.html /usr/share/nginx/html
ADD=to copy the files and folders local machine to Docker container and web pages also copy download using urls
ex: ADD https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.71/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.71.tar.gz  .
EXPOSE= to set port numbers
ex: EXPOSE 8080
ENV=to set the environment variables
ex: ENV name =venkat
   ENV password =challa
