🛡️ Troubleshooting Port/Connection Issues – Real-Time Examples
🔍 1. 🔒 EC2 Instance - SSH Not Working (Port 22)
Scenario: You can’t SSH into your EC2 instance.
Checklist:
✅ Is port 22 open in Security Group?
✅ Is the NACL blocking traffic?
✅ Is the EC2 running?
✅ Is the correct key pair being used?
✅ Is the public IP correct?
Commands:
telnet <ec2-public-ip> 22 # OR nc -zv <ec2-public-ip> 22

🌐 2. 🌍 Website Not Loading on HTTP/HTTPS (80/443)
Scenario: Your web app isn't loading.
Checklist:
Is EC2's SG/NACL allowing 80/443?
Is the web server (Apache/Nginx) running?
Is the correct listener added in the Load Balancer?
Check Route 53 DNS settings.
Commands:
curl -I http://<public-ip>
curl -I https://<domain-name>

🐳 3. Docker Container Not Accessible on Host Port
Scenario:You expose a Docker container on port 8080, but can't access it.
Checklist:
Is Docker container port mapped correctly (-p 8080:8080)?
Is the firewall (ufw/iptables) allowing that port?
Is the container running and app bound to 0.0.0.0?
Command:
docker ps
sudo netstat -tulnp | grep 8080
curl http://localhost:8080
🧰 4. Jenkins Not Opening on Port 8080
Scenario: Jenkins UI not loading.
Checklist:
Is Jenkins service running?
Is the instance's SG/NACL/Firewall open for 8080?
Is Jenkins listening on correct IP?
Command:
sudo systemctl status jenkins
sudo netstat -plnt | grep 8080
curl http://localhost:8080
🛜 5. Kubernetes Pod Not Accessible (NodePort / Ingress)
Scenario: NodePort/Ingress service unreachable.
Checklist:
Is 30000–32767 range allowed in Security Group?
Is the Pod healthy and running?
Is the Service correctly defined (type: NodePort)?
Are nodes reachable?
Command:
kubectl get svc
kubectl get pods -o wide
curl <node-ip>:<nodeport>
🔐 6. S3 Access Denied
Scenario: “Access Denied” error when uploading to S3.
Checklist:
Check IAM role permissions (s3:PutObject, etc.)
Check Bucket Policy
Check if block public access is on
Command:
aws s3 cp file.txt s3://my-bucket/ --profile <your-profile>
🧱 7. Security Group Blocks App Communication
Scenario: Microservices can’t talk to each other (e.g., app to DB on port 3306).
Checklist:
SG of target (DB) must allow inbound from source SG on 3306.
Check NACL between subnets.
Use telnet or nc to test connection.
Command:
nc -zv <db-private-ip> 3306
📊 8. Prometheus Cannot Scrape Metrics from Target
Scenario: Prometheus target shows as DOWN.
Checklist:
Is the target port open?
Is the target metrics endpoint correct (/metrics)?
Are firewalls allowing access?
Command:
curl http://<target-ip>:<port>/metrics
🧪 9. Lambda in VPC Cannot Reach Internet
Scenario: Lambda can't call external APIs.
Checklist:
Is Lambda in private subnet?
Does the subnet have NAT Gateway + route table?
Is security group/NACL open?
📩 10. SNS Email Not Received
Scenario: Email not received after SNS topic publish.
Checklist:
Did user confirm subscription?
Is SNS in right region?
Check email filters/spam.
