AWS Interview Questions and Answers (50+ Q&A for 1–2 Years Experience)
🔹 EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)
What is EC2 and its primary use?
EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) is a virtual server in AWS used to run applications on the cloud. It provides scalable computing capacity.
What is the difference between AMI and Snapshot?
AMI is an image used to launch EC2 instances (includes OS + app config), while a Snapshot is a backup of an EBS volume.
How do you secure an EC2 instance?
By configuring Security Groups, using key pairs (SSH), enabling IAM roles, and regularly patching the OS.
What is a Security Group vs NACL?
Security Groups act as firewalls at the instance level (stateful). NACLs operate at subnet level (stateless).
What is the difference between EBS and Instance Store?
EBS is persistent storage; data remains after stopping instance. Instance Store is ephemeral and deleted when the instance stops.

🔹 S3 (Simple Storage Service)
What is S3 and its storage classes?
S3 is an object storage service. Classes: Standard, Intelligent-Tiering, One Zone-IA, Glacier, Deep Archive.
How does versioning in S3 work?
Enables multiple versions of objects, protects against accidental deletes or overwrites.
Explain S3 bucket policies vs IAM policies.
Bucket policies control access to specific S3 buckets. IAM policies are attached to users/roles to control access to all AWS resources.
How can you make an S3 bucket publicly accessible?
Set bucket policy to allow public access and disable "Block all public access" settings.
What are pre-signed URLs in S3?
URLs that allow temporary access to private S3 objects, generated with IAM credentials.

🔹 IAM (Identity and Access Management)
What is IAM? Why is it important?
IAM lets you manage users, roles, and permissions securely. It controls who can access AWS resources.
Difference between IAM Role and IAM User?
IAM User is a specific person/account. IAM Role is a set of permissions assigned temporarily (used by services, other AWS accounts).
What is the use of policies in IAM?
Policies define permissions. They are attached to users, roles, or groups to allow/deny specific actions.
What is the principle of least privilege?
Grant only the minimum permissions required to perform a task.
How do you enable MFA on IAM users?
Through IAM dashboard > Users > Security credentials > Enable MFA > Assign a virtual MFA device.

🔹 VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)
What is a VPC in AWS?
A logically isolated network in AWS where you launch your resources. You control IP ranges, subnets, route tables, etc.
Difference between public and private subnet?
Public subnet has route to internet via Internet Gateway; private subnet doesn’t.
What is an Internet Gateway and NAT Gateway?
IGW provides internet access for public subnets. NAT Gateway allows private subnet instances to access the internet securely.
What are Route Tables and how do they work?
Determine traffic direction in the VPC. Each subnet must be associated with a route table.
What is a VPC Peering Connection?
A private connection between two VPCs to enable traffic between them without using internet.

🔹 CloudWatch & Monitoring
What is Amazon CloudWatch?
It monitors AWS resources and applications. Offers metrics, logs, dashboards, and alarms.
Difference between CloudWatch and CloudTrail?
CloudWatch: monitors performance. CloudTrail: logs API calls for auditing.
How do you create a CloudWatch alarm?
Choose a metric, set a threshold, define an action (e.g., send SNS email or trigger auto-scaling).
Can you monitor custom metrics in CloudWatch?
Yes, you can push custom metrics using AWS CLI or SDK.
What is the use of CloudWatch Logs?
To collect and store logs from EC2, Lambda, ECS, etc., and monitor them in real-time.

🔹 Lambda & Serverless
What is AWS Lambda?
Serverless compute service that runs code in response to events (no need to provision servers).
What are cold starts in Lambda?
Delay that occurs when Lambda initializes a new container (first time or after idle period).
How does Lambda integrate with API Gateway?
API Gateway acts as a trigger and forwards HTTP requests to Lambda functions.
What is the timeout limit in Lambda?
Maximum timeout for Lambda is 15 minutes.
How do you manage Lambda versions and aliases?
You can publish versions and create aliases to manage deployment environments (dev, test, prod).

🔹 RDS & Databases
What is Amazon RDS?
Managed relational database service. Supports MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, MariaDB, Oracle.
Difference between RDS and DynamoDB?
RDS is relational, DynamoDB is NoSQL (key-value and document database).
What is Multi-AZ in RDS?
Creates a standby replica in another AZ for failover and high availability.
How does RDS backup work?
Automated daily snapshots and transaction logs. You can restore to any point within the retention period.
Can you access RDS from outside VPC?
Yes, if the DB is in a public subnet and security groups allow access from your IP.

🔹 CloudFormation & IAC
What is AWS CloudFormation?
An infrastructure as code service that lets you model and provision AWS resources using YAML/JSON templates.
Difference between template and stack?
Template is the blueprint (YAML/JSON). Stack is a deployed instance of that template.
How does CloudFormation handle rollbacks?
If resource creation fails, CloudFormation rolls back all changes by default.
Can you update a stack without downtime?
Yes, using Change Sets and Update policies.
What is drift detection?
Detects if stack resources have changed outside of CloudFormation.

🔹 SQS, SNS & Messaging
What is Amazon SQS?
A managed message queue service. Supports standard and FIFO queues.
Difference between SQS and SNS?
SQS is pull-based (queue), SNS is push-based (pub/sub model).
What is FIFO Queue?
First-In-First-Out queue in SQS that ensures exactly-once processing.
How do dead-letter queues work?
Captures messages that fail processing after a threshold number of attempts.
How can you trigger Lambda from SNS?
Subscribe a Lambda function to an SNS topic. When the topic receives a message, it invokes the function.

🔹 DevOps & CI/CD
What is AWS CodePipeline?
A CI/CD service that automates build, test, and deploy phases.
Difference between CodeDeploy and CodeBuild?
CodeBuild compiles and tests code. CodeDeploy handles automated deployment.
How do you use Git with AWS?
