5) i have a target group using that target group i use only one server other we can set wetting period or not?
Yes, in AWS Target Groups, you can set a waiting period before considering a target (like your EC2 server) as healthy or unhealthy — this is done through health check settings, not a “waiting period” in the traditional sense, but functionally similar.
✅ Your Setup:
You have a Target Group (used with ALB/NLB).
It points to one EC2 instance.
You want to ensure that other instances wait before receiving traffic, or control when they start receiving traffic.
✅ What You Can Control in Target Group:
🔹 1. Health Check Grace Period (for Auto Scaling)
If you’re using Auto Scaling, you can configure a Health Check Grace Period:
Gives the instance time to boot and become ready.
Until then, ALB won’t send traffic.
🔧 Set this in Auto Scaling Group settings, not Target Group directly.
🔹 2. Deregistration Delay (Drain Time)
When removing a target (instance), AWS waits for N seconds before stopping traffic.
Default: 300 seconds
Controls how long existing connections are allowed to drain
Set in: Target Group settings → Attributes → Deregistration delay
🔧 Useful for controlled shutdown or updates.
🔹 3. Health Check Settings
This is where you can indirectly control waiting behavior:
Healthy Threshold: Number of successes before traffic starts
Unhealthy Threshold: Failures before traffic stops
Interval: How often to check (e.g., every 30s)
Timeout: Max time the app has to respond
Success Code: What response is considered "healthy" (default 200)
📌 Idea: Set these so your new app version or new instance gets a grace period before it's considered ready.
🔄 Example Use Case
You have:
App1 on instance A (healthy, serving traffic)
App2 on instance B (new, should wait before serving)
✅ Use Health Check settings on the Target Group:
Interval: 30s
Healthy threshold: 5
Total wait = 30s × 5 = 150s before considered healthy
✅ Optional: Set Deregistration delay to 60s, so old instances finish serving users cleanly.
🧠 Summary
Feature
Use
Health Check Threshold
Wait before considering target healthy
Health Check Grace Period
Delay health checks for new EC2 in ASG
Deregistration Delay
Wait before removing target from ALB
Sticky Sessions (Optional)
Keep user on same instance


