✅ 13) Did you deploy a full-fledged application? Give start-to-end process.
Yes. Here's a real-world deployment process for a full-stack web app:
Requirement gathering: Understand tech stack (e.g., React + Node.js + MongoDB).
Provision VPC: Create VPC with public/private subnets, internet gateway, route tables.
Create EC2 Instances: Launch in private subnet, use public subnet for Bastion host or ALB.
Configure security groups: Allow HTTP/HTTPS, SSH from limited IP.
Use RDS: Create managed DB if needed.
Store static files in S3.
Deploy code: CI/CD using CodePipeline (GitHub → CodeBuild → EC2).
Use Application Load Balancer: For traffic distribution.
Attach SSL using ACM.
Monitoring: CloudWatch, CloudTrail, X-Ray for performance & security.
Backup and scaling: Auto scaling & RDS snapshots.
DNS: Use Route 53 for custom domain.

✅ 14) If S3 bucket full access public – is it OK or not?
❌ No, it’s not okay.
 A fully public S3 bucket means anyone can read, write, or delete your data — this can lead to data leaks or even ransomware attacks. Even you want use sse-kms and sse-s3 encryption use

✅ 15) Client needs S3 bucket public — how do you secure it?
If public access is absolutely needed:
Restrict via Bucket Policy: Allow only specific IPs or VPC endpoints.
Enable Object Lock: Prevent overwrite/deletion.
Enable Logging: Enable S3 access logs to monitor usage.
Use Signed URLs or Signed Cookies.
Apply MFA Delete.
Use CloudFront: Expose only via CDN with caching & geo-blocking.

✅ 16) Did you use VPC Site-to-Site VPN and Direct Connect? Explain.
Yes.
Site-to-Site VPN:
Connects on-premises datacenter to AWS over encrypted public internet.
Uses Virtual Private Gateway + Customer Gateway.
IPsec tunnel; quick to set up.
Direct Connect:
Dedicated private connection from on-prem to AWS (bypass internet).
More secure, faster, and stable.
Used for high-throughput, low-latency, sensitive workloads.

✅ 17) Did you create a full VPC? What are the steps & VPC properties?
Yes. Steps:
Create VPC (CIDR block, e.g., 10.0.0.0/16)
Create Subnets (e.g., 2 public, 2 private)
Create Internet Gateway and attach to VPC
Create Route Tables
Associate subnets with route tables
Create NAT Gateway for private subnet internet access
Create Security Groups and NACLs
Configure VPC endpoints if needed
Properties:
CIDR, DNS support, DHCP options, Tenancy, Flow logs, IPv6

✅ 18) One app deployed but some users must be blocked – how to block without WAF?
