✅ 23) Security team reports data leak — how do you detect & resolve it?
Steps:
Check CloudTrail logs: Who accessed what, when.
Enable S3 access logs / VPC Flow Logs.
Use GuardDuty: Detect anomalies like unusual IPs, malware activity.
Use Macie: Detect sensitive data leaked (e.g., PII, credentials).
Block public access: S3, EC2 ports, IAM keys.
Rotate secrets / keys.
Review IAM roles: Least privilege principle.
Use AWS Config: See changes to resources and who made them.
Preventive Measures:
Enable versioning & object lock (for S3)
Use centralized logging (CloudWatch, SIEM)
Regularly run AWS Inspector / vulnerability tools
